Le 05.11.2003 14:08:19, Vincenzo Forchi` a écrit :
>
> xavier grave wrote
>
> > Hi everybody,
> >
> > We just have received a new mvmv5500 from motorola.
> > It runs with linux-2.4.20 kernel (std tree) + motorola patches.
>
> hi,
> did you use netBoot to get the kernel?
> I'm trying with 2.4.20+motorola patches but it doesn't seem to work.
> can you post your .config? I think it's something with the galileo
> chip
>
In order to boot I use the following command :
netBoot -s192.168.120.70 -s192.168.120.75 -fzImage.pplus -z

the -z option is really important (don't boot)

I send you three kind of config, there are few differences between
them.
There is a surprise : the device 0 in MOTLoad -> eth1
		      the device 1 in MOTLoad -> eth0

So you should try in first attemp the config_test_ipnpwpc5_eth1 file.

Hope it will help...

xavier
--YiEDa0DAkWCtVeE4
